  "summary": "A 19-year-old San Diego man and the owner of the vehicle he was riding in have filed tort claims alleging a San Diego Police officer shot him after an ALPR hotlist alert falsely identified the car as stolen. The claims come as a San Diego City Council committee signaled willingness to end the city's Flock Safety contract.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "The Department's ALPR system automatically receives stolen-vehicle information from [the National Crime Information Center] through regularly updated hotlists",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    },
    {
      "quote": "The officer exited his vehicle, gave no verbal commands, and immediately fired one round from his firearm",
